This file is a placeholder example, not a live recall source.

By default every human prompt gets a recall block from the knowledge graph
(data/memory/graph.db); you do not need this file for that.

Copy this to config/recall-source (or point KARAKOS_RECALL_SOURCE at a copy
elsewhere) only to OVERRIDE the graph: when either exists, the graph is not
consulted and this source is used instead. A plain file is read verbatim on
every UserPromptSubmit turn; an executable file receives the pending prompt
on stdin and its stdout becomes the recall block. See docs/EXTENDING.md,
"Recall re-injection".

config/recall-source does not exist by default, so inject-recall.py uses the
graph until an operator acts on this.
